  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.5.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: tailcat\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/tailscale/tailcat/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: a2177d257ac7a02d8ba0fdfcfa341113d97ea0cf7597dbb0fff851d8c341d8e9\n  target_directory: src\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    - cd src\n    # build-tags.txt is a single comma-separated line of the build tags the\n    # official releases use; see build-tags.md. Building without them still\n    # works, it only makes the binary larger.\n    - if: unix\n      then:\n        - go-licenses save ./cmd/tailcat --save_path ../library_licenses\n        - go build -v -o $PREFIX/bin/tailcat -tags \"$(cat build-tags.txt)\" -ldflags=\"-s -w -X main.version=v${{ version }}\" ./cmd/tailcat\n      else:\n        - go-licenses save ./cmd/tailcat --save_path ../library_licenses\n        - set /p TAGS=<build-tags.txt\n        - go build -v -o %PREFIX%\\bin\\tailcat.exe -tags \"%TAGS%\" -ldflags=\"-s -X main.version=v${{ version }}\" ./cmd/tailcat\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler(\"go-nocgo\") }}\n    - go-licenses\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - tailcat --version\n      - tailcat --help\n      - tailcat version\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - tailcat\n      strict: true\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/tailscale/tailcat\n  summary: Like netcat, but over Tailscale's data plane, without Tailscale's control plane\n  description: |\n    Tailcat is a remix of Tailscale open source pieces to act like netcat, but\n    over Tailscale's data plane, without Tailscale's control plane. Tailscale's\n    data plane gives you point-to-point WireGuard-encrypted tunnels between two\n    machines with DERP as the NAT-hole-punching communication side channel and\n    the relay of last resort if NAT traversal fails. Instead of using the\n    Tailscale control plane, all tailcat connection metadata is exchanged out of\n    band, however you want.\n\n    One side runs a tailcat server (listener) and gets back a short connection\n    token. The other side passes that token to tailcat's client side to connect.\n    All traffic between the two is encrypted end-to-end with WireGuard.\n\n    No Tailscale account and no root/admin access are required; tailcat does not\n    alter the machine's routing tables or DNS.\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file:\n    - src/LICENSE\n    - library_licenses/\n  documentation: https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/tailscale/tailcat\n  repository: https://github.com/tailscale/tailcat\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - pavelzw\n",
